Code shared with PJA
--------------------

pas/praarith.pas (binary arithmetic coder), pas/prablake3.pas (BLAKE3),
pas/praformat.pas (the container), pas/prafs.pas (verified writing),
pas/pracpu.pas, pas/pracli.pas (the command, adapted), pas/collisions.py and
the tests of those units (test_arith, test_blake3, test_format, test_prafs,
cli.sh, adapted) come from PJA (github.com/YadeWira/PJA, MIT, same author).
BLAKE3 follows its specification (github.com/BLAKE3-team/BLAKE3-specs).

packPNM
-------

PRA is the spiritual successor of packPNM by Matthias Stirner (LGPLv3). It
takes ideas from it, not code.

PPA's deflate layer
-------------------

vendor/ppa (the units ppapreflate, ppadeflate, ppazlib, ppaminiz, ppacorr,
ppacrc, ppaarith, ppathreads, ppajoin, ppa.inc and the C files beside them)
is PPA's deflate layer, copied as it is from the release tarball of PPA
0.3.0 (github.com/YadeWira/PPA, tag v0.3.0, commit 8370a31; MIT, same
author); vendor/ppa/SHA256SUMS has the tarball's hash of each file. It
gives back a deflate stream bit for bit from the bytes it holds and a
recipe. Its third-party notes (zlib's and miniz's choices ported, the idea
of preflate) are in vendor/ppa/NOTICE.
